  "why_not_the_826_mm2_frame": "a ROM product holds its weights on die, so it is larger than a GPU die by construction -- 16 GiB is 946 mm2 at the optimistic density. Asking what it achieves inside 826 mm2 answers a question about packaging, not about the design. Matched silicon area is the comparison the roofline already makes and the one the architecture is for."
